#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:191
msgid ""
"TMEM is a dedicated on-chip memory introduced in Hopper GPUs, designed to "
"reduce register pressure and enable asynchronous, single-threaded MMA "
"operations. It is organized as a 2D array of 512 columns by 128 rows "
"(lanes), with each cell being 32 bits. Allocation is performed in units of "
"columns, and every lane of a column is allocated together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:193
msgid "Key properties and requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:194
msgid "The number of columns allocated must be a power of 2 and at least 32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:195
msgid ""
"TMEM allocations are dynamic. TileLang deallocates them automatically at the "
"end of the allocation block unless you call ``T.deallocate_tmem`` to take "
"manual control of the lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:198
msgid "Both allocation and deallocation must be performed by the same warp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:199
msgid ""
"The base address of the TMEM allocation is stored in shared memory and used "
"as the offset for TCGEN5.MMA accumulator tensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:200
msgid ""
"Only TCGEN5.MMA and specific TMEM load/store instructions can access TMEM; "
"all pre-processing must occur before data is loaded into TMEM, and all post-"
"processing after data is retrieved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:201
msgid ""
"The number of columns allocated should not increase between any two "
"allocations in the execution order within the CTA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:203
msgid ""
"Number of columns to allocate in TMEM. Must be a power of 2 and >= 32 but "
"less than or equal to 512."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:206
msgid ""
"A TVM buffer object allocated in TMEM scope, suitable for use as an "
"accumulator or operand in TCGEN5.MMA operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:211
msgid ""
"TMEM is only available on supported architectures (e.g., Hopper and later)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:212
msgid ""
"The buffer returned should be used according to TMEM access restrictions. "
"Use ``T.deallocate_tmem`` only when you need an earlier, explicit release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:222
msgid ""
"Modifications needs to conform with `op`, such as `op=\"sum\"` requires "
"`reducer[...] += ...` and `op=\"max\"` requires `reducer[...] = T."
"max(reducer[...], ...)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:226
msgid ""
"Only after T.fill with proper initializer the reduction may begin; only "
"after T.finalize_reducer the partial results will be available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:229
msgid ""
"For `op=\"sum\"`, filled value must be 0; for min and max, the filled "
"initializer will become max or min clamper correspondingly. You may want to "
"use `T.max_value` for min and `T.min_value` for max."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:236
msgid "The reduce operation corresponded with the reducer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:238
msgid ""
"Replication strategy, can be \"all\" or \"none\". Defaults to not specified, "
"and the compiler will do whatever it want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:241
msgid ""
"A TVM buffer object allocated in thread-private storage, available to reduce "
"values in T.Parallel loops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:251
msgid ""
"The descriptor kind, one of \"wgmma\", \"tcgen05\" (\"utcmma\" as alias)."
